# What tests/check-path-buffers.sh lets stand.  Five kinds of line (NUMBER,
# SENTENCE and COPY below; PROJECTWORDS and GUESS before COPY):
#
#   NUMBER|name|reason
#       A #define whose name ends like a path number (PATH_MAX, DIR_MAX,
#       NAME_MAX ...) and is not one: a function's name, a count of folders.
#       A line that matches no define is stale.
#
#   SENTENCE|file|reason
#       A string literal that says a path is longer than something, which is
#       another owner's sentence and not WPE_PATH_TOO_LONG_FMT.
#
#   COPY|file|function|count|kind|reason
#       The strcpy, strcat, strncpy and sprintf calls of a function.  "count"
#       may only fall.  "kind" says why the calls stand:
#         sized    the destination is allocated at the length of its sources
#                  just before, or by the caller, who passes the sources' size
#         text     a fixed text, or a bounded string, into a larger array
#         checked  the length is tested against the array before the copy
#       No kind is "path": a path that fits none of these goes through the
#       owner (wpe_path_copy, _join, _cat, _dup, _join_dup), which refuses a
#       path that does not fit instead of running past the array or cutting it.
#       The calls below were read at the pass that wrote this file; "sized"
#       says the allocation is next to the copy, not that every site was
#       measured under a sanitizer.

# --- NUMBER: not a path ---
NUMBER|WPE_AI_PROVIDER_NAME_MAX|the longest name of an assistant provider
NUMBER|WPE_HOST_ADD_DIR_MAX|how many folders the hosted assistant may be given
NUMBER|E_DAP_FRAME_NAME_MAX|a function's name in a stack frame
NUMBER|E_D_REQ_NAME_MAX|a debugger's name in a notice
NUMBER|E_DS_NAME_MAX|a function, a signal or a class of a debug session
NUMBER|E_D_JDB_EXCEPTION_NAME_MAX|the name of an exception class in jdb's words
NUMBER|E_D_FRAME_NAME_MAX|a function's name in the Stack window
NUMBER|E_LSP_NAME_MAX|the name of a language server's menu entry
NUMBER|E_BUFFER_FAULT_NAME_MAX|the name of a buffer fault in the trace
NUMBER|E_ESV_MIN_NAME_MAX|the shortest file name the emergency save needs

# --- SENTENCE: another owner's words about a path's length ---
SENTENCE|we_ai_ui.c|the assistant's fix-build line: the file's path does not go into a command
SENTENCE|we_debug.c|the debugger's own line when a file path does not fit its request
SENTENCE|we_startplan.h|the start plan's reason for refusing a folder or program

# --- PROJECTWORDS and GUESS: the system's reason is said, not guessed ---
# PROJECTWORDS|file|function|reason
#     The one function that holds the words "Project file not found" and
#     "Cannot open project": no other function says the project did not open.
#     A line whose function holds none of them is stale.
# GUESS|file|function|pass-or-keep|reason
#     A function that asks the system about a path (access, stat, fopen ...)
#     and holds a "not found" or "cannot open" string without errno or
#     strerror.  "keep" says why the words are not about that path; a pass
#     names the design that moves the site onto the owner of the system's
#     reason.  A line that matches no such function is stale.
PROJECTWORDS|we_prog.c|e_prj_say_not_opened|the reporter: ENOENT says not found, every other errno says the system's reason
GUESS|we_progn.c|e_show_nm_f|keep|the word is about the symbol searched; the access only chooses the project's files over the window's
GUESS|we_startplan.c|startplan_embedded_file|read-refused|"(not found)" stands for any failed access of the script file; the read side's owner takes it over

# --- COPY ---
